// Spier and Hepner follow the Bracke precedent (SDAP leaders). Jacoby was a
// radical democrat of 1848 who joined the SDAP only in 1872 and rejected class
// struggle. Ferry and Simon led the moderate/Opportunist republicans (Favre,
// Gambetta, Freycinet precedent). Gramont owed his career to Louis Napoleon
// and served the Empire (Napoleon III precedent). Flourens was close to the
// Blanquists (Blanqui precedent). The Vendéan leaders follow Charette and
// Stofflet. No collection: Bourbaki, Benedetti (soldier/diplomat of the
// Empire), Ollivier (republican turned Liberal-Empire minister, later
// Bonapartist: ambiguous), Haxo and Canclaux (Kléber/Marceau precedent).
